## 1. Q1 — K16: what structurally forces B·W'(0) = 0, one new mechanism, cheapest decisive test

### 1.1 The top-down recursion of (F3) is resonance-free for t ≥ 3 (desk-verified; KNOWN in substance)

Put Z = xW − r (r = b²/4). Astra's (F3) becomes, after multiplying by x²,

    x·(Z²)′ − 3Z² = (B − 2A + D)·x·Z + R(x),
    R = −3r² + x·r·(D − 3B) + x²·[A(A−D)/3 − B(A−D) − bηK/(2y) − Bηx],

with Z of degree 2t+2, Z_{2t+2} = ω, Z_0 = −r, Z_1 = −B, Z_2 = η, and A = αx³C² (α = 3/(4y²)). Reading
the coefficient of x^{4t+4−j} gives a triangular recursion in which Z_{2t+2−j} enters linearly with
pivot p_j = 2ω(4t+1−j) + 2α, everything else being higher Z's, the C-coefficients, B, b, η. With
ω = α(2d−1)/(4t+1) and 4t+1 = 3(2d−1)(2d+1), the pivot vanishes iff j = 6d(2d+1). For d > 0 this
exceeds 2t+2; for d = −δ it equals 4t+4−6δ, inside [0, 2t+2] iff δ = 1, i.e. t = 2, at j = 6 = 2t+2,
the Z_0 closing pivot. Astra's y = (d+t+1)/(2q) puts that fibre at y = 1/5 — the banked (8.1)-holds /
(V0)-fails fibre, and Opus's "the failure is exactly a₀ = 0" is this same pivot (a₀ is the leading
coefficient of the top row, quadratic in b3). `box/ideation0200-fable5-20260905/abel_pivots.py` checks
the formula, the fibre values (t=2: 1/5, 2/5; t=11: 5/23, 7/23; t=26: 12/53, 15/53) and the leading
balance; output banked in `abel_pivots.out`.

Consequence, and why it matters for the proof shape: by the positive weights (wt x = 1, wt c_i =
t−1−i, wt b = t+1, wt B = 2t+1, wt η = 2t, wt Z_k = 2t+2−k) the recursed Z_3, …, Z_{2t+1} are polynomials
in (c, b) ALONE — B and η have weights too large to appear — and the three closing equations at
j = 2t, 2t+1, 2t+2 then read: p_{2t}·η = P₂(c,b), p_{2t+1}·(−B) = P₁(c,b,η), p_{2t+2}·(−b²/4) = P₀(c,b,η,B).
So η and B are POLYNOMIAL FUNCTIONS of (c,b) for t ≥ 3 (unit pivots), the last closing equation is the
quadratic top row in b, and the remaining low equations are the rest of I_{t,+} in the t variables
(c_0..c_{t−2}, b) with 2t−1 generators. This is exactly the banked terminal ideal (Astra's
ABEL_ROW_IDENTITY_PASS), so the Abel form adds no new equation; what it adds is the STATEMENT SHAPE:

> (8.1)_t ⟺ the weighted-homogeneous ideal I_{t,+} ⊂ A_t[c,b] (2t−1 generators, t variables,
> weights (t−1,…,1,t+1)) contains a power of the single polynomial τ_t ∝ B(c,b)·η(c,b), where η is
> the weight-2t and B the weight-(2t+1) closing polynomial.

