Here NF_Z is literal polynomial remainder in the declared field[x], with omega inverted as a scalar unit. To prove the converse, put D=Psi/Z-H. Differentiation of Psi=Z(Psi/Z) shows that (Q1.5) implies Z divides Z'D. Squarefreeness gives Z divides D. The leading balance gives deg D<n_Z, so D=0. At a root a of multiplicity m>1, the exact replacement is **all m quotient jets** of D at a; (Q1.5) alone retains only part of them. The collision-inclusive formulation is D=0 in k[x]/(Z), again with deg D<n_Z. A prospective proof must work in that local algebra or retain the corresponding Hasse derivatives.

The strongest proof attack is therefore: show that **no normalized half-degree divisor of this linked Psi can satisfy its differential cofactor conditions when B*eta!=0**, using the fixed quartic's ramification and the constrained graph w=Byx/(bK). The bounded obstruction is the n_Z-dimensional remainder vector, augmented by the full multiplicity jets when needed. The target is zero admissible divisors for every t>=3 and each normalizer factor. This remains OPEN. The cover stratification is the new mechanism; it is not a proof that the target vector is nonzero.

