/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:7:## 1. Decisions first, and disposition changes
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:9:**The packet overstates both the finite residual and the all-degree compression.** The first correction helps: two of its fourteen excess rows already die under the promoted Xu screen, leaving **twelve rows in six full characteristic-data classes**, before consuming anything from the running Opus lane. The second correction costs: the actual sharpened u_s>=2 cohort compresses **296 -> 132**, not approximately 65, on the proposed four-integer key. That key also merges different inherited characteristic sequences. A kill can still be shared through a proved common necessary receiver, but equality of four integers is not that proof.
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:11:**K16 is one precise atom on one prototype. It is not the unique structural gap of the programme.** Neither a finite census nor one cofinal family supplies an all-degree covering theorem. The single most valuable next object is a **certificate-bearing receiver atlas**: an explicit source-to-receiver map for every branch being charged, with an honest UNASSIGNED output. Its first finite test is already available: the sharpened 296-row cohort, its 132 coarse keys, and its higher-depth collisions. This should precede a large class sweep. The finite Moh closure can continue alongside it.
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:19:| 1 — Newton/monomial-Jacobian receivers | **raise** | Move construction and transfer of necessary receiver equations ahead of a raw class farm. The finite Moh residue is now twelve, but all twelve have descended depth greater than two. The 296-row audit exhibits coarse-key collisions before any split geometry. This is a concrete correctness and amortization problem for the main receiver engine. |
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:20:| 2 — boundary/tree route | **raise** | Give total routing and receiver coverage an explicit proof allocation. First-separation and route-to-state cannot be collapsed into integer invariants or a finite list of successful arrivals. This is a separate interface obligation from Moh's already-sourced split/radius alternative. |
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:25:Proof allocation: **finite Moh closure**, **receiver coverage**, **K16 truncation**, then an **all-degree covering/termination theorem**. This is an expenditure order, not an implication chain. Global reduction interfaces have greater logical scope than K16. Falsification allocation: break a claimed source-to-receiver map first; seek an exact normalized B*eta!=0 point second; only an actual polynomial Keller lift supplies a disproof. A modular or necessary-chart survivor does not. Avenues 19/21 retain their bounded-support obligation; no fresh reason was found to restart stopped implication ladders, bare passports or ordinary exact-form residues.
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:29:## 2. Q1 — attack differential-compatible factors of a linked quartic
/tmp/jc2-lane.MMCkx9/inputs/ideation-20260905T0200Z-astra.md:45:### 2.1 A polynomial identity, with no root divisions
